From: Charles Hoskinson <charles.hoskinson@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:18:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] E4: GPU fractional sumcheck hook for the Fr config

StarkProtocolConfig::frac_gkr_accel (default None) gives fractional_sumcheck an
optional FracGkrAccel: the segment tree and each GKR layer sumcheck (round polynomial
at 1, 2, 3 and the fold, with the transcript kept in Rust through a callback). The Fr
config implements it under the stark-sdk feature gpu with mori-gpu frac for layers of
at least 2^12 points; E4_GPU_FRAC=0 takes the CPU path. Field arithmetic is exact, so
the L_Fr proof is byte-identical to the CPU proof.
